crates/audio-playback and crates/ui/src/player
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adapted from filmcraft (https://github.com/spdrman/filmcraft).

    filmcraft
    Copyright (c) 2026 the filmcraft authors.
    Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at our
    option; used here under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Each file below names its origin in its own header.

  crates/audio-playback/src/ring.rs
      Adapted from filmcraft's `crates/ui-egui/src/play_ahead.rs`. The
      single-producer/single-consumer ring of atomically stored f32 bit
      patterns, the lead-buffer mixing thread, and the underrun "play silence
      and make the mixer skip the same frames" accounting are filmcraft's
      design and implementation. Renamed types, `tracing` instead of `log`,
      the `serde_json` statistics export removed, and new tests.

  crates/audio-playback/src/cpal_out.rs
      Structure follows filmcraft's `CpalOut` (`apps/filmcraft/src/audio.rs`):
      an atomic played-frame counter as the master clock, `catch_unwind`
      around the mixer inside the device callback, sample-format conversion
      with clamping, and a health record fed by cpal's error callback.
      Rewritten against cpal 0.18; no filmcraft code is copied verbatim.

  crates/ui/src/player/waveform.rs
      The painting technique — one `egui::Mesh` of one-point-wide coloured
      rectangles, folded per pixel column from (min, max) buckets — is the one
      filmcraft uses in its timeline and source-monitor waveforms. The
      implementation here is new: it reads a multiresolution pyramid rather
      than a single-resolution bucket list.

